==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[heart]] [[attack]]}}

# {{cardiology|pathology}} Acute [[myocardial infarction]] that is the sudden occurrence of [[coronary thrombosis]] which obstructs the blood supply to the heart resulting in [[necrosis]] of heart muscle.  It is characterised by sudden severe chest pain often radiating  to the shoulder, arm, or jaw, shortness of breath, [[nausea]], loss of consciousness, and sometimes resulting in death.

====Synonyms====
* [[myocardial infarction]]

